  "text": "She prayed so hard the priest told her to sober up. She had not touched a drink. Elkanah has two wives. Peninnah has children. Hannah does not. And Scripture calls Peninnah her adversary, and says she provoked her sore. Year after year. Every single time they went up to worship. At the one place she goes to meet God. So Hannah stops eating and weeps. And her husband, who genuinely loves her, says the most well meaning wrong thing in the Bible: \"Am not I better to thee than ten sons?\" Sir. Read the room. So she gets up from that table and goes to the house of the Lord. And she prays in bitterness of soul. Here is the detail. She spake in her heart. Only her lips moved. Her voice was not heard. And Eli the priest, whose entire job is recognising devotion when he sees it, watches her mouth move and decides she is drunk. Out loud. \"How long wilt thou be drunken? Put away thy wine from thee.\" And Hannah does not shrink and does not fight. \"No, my lord, I am a woman of a sorrowful spirit: I have drunken neither wine nor strong drink, but have poured out my soul before the LORD.\" The most honest prayer in the building. And the priest called her a drunk. She walks out still childless. And the text says her countenance was no more sad.",
